Spec: Revocation capacity reservation

Purpose:
  Keep one retained-operation slot available for revoking each approved local declaration within hard journal bounds.

Owns:
  ./JournalCapacity.cs

References:
  ./RegistrationStore.sdd
  ./RegistrationReview.sdd
  /docs/adr/0010-revocation-capacity.md

Must:
  Include exact local visitor grants in schema validation and reserved revocation accounting; peer revocation atomically retires both publisher and visitor authority.
  Count each approved declaration as one reserved slot in both global and host operation budgets.
  Count active secure devices and service grants as reserved revocations and include their administrator journal in host usage.
  Admit a new approval only when its result and future revocation fit; ordinary mutations cannot consume reserved slots.
  Consume an existing reservation and retain the revocation result atomically, without bypassing quotas or deleting prior operations.
  Derive reservations from durable approved state after restart and expose only host-local aggregate capacity diagnostics.
  Reject migration or admission when retained results plus reservations exceed configured limits.
  Keep storage failures, stale decisions and integer exhaustion distinct from the logical quota guarantee.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify full-budget revocation, concurrent admission, rollback and schema migration.
